gs school  is still here we're stronger than ever  and we're going to rebuild but even with  the support of their neighbors the  clerks say the devastation may be too  great to overcome do you have family or  anyone who can pick you up and fit you  with them  no not really no  my whole family's in dawson so  everybody lost their own homes yeah  we're hoping to stay in dawson i'd  rather stay in dawson  but  honestly at this point we don't have  many options  state officials say more than 600 people  are now sheltered in those seven parks  in the state many people are in the same  situation as that family and we spoke to  that pre-k teacher that preschool  teacher what she says is that now she's  starting to worry about the community's  mental health she says this area is so  prone to severe weather and all she can  think of is how those children and their  parents are going to start reacting when  they hear thunder or strong winds like  the ones we've been having over the last  two days tony  yeah the recovery goes on lilia thank  you great reporting this week from a  tough story out of kentucky
 

